  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV testing and Counselling (HTC) in Malawi-Lighthouse</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lighthouse would like to increase the number of HIV testing and counselling, by increasing the individual sites of Maula prison, community HTC which form part of the Lighthouse&apos;s  linkage with Archdiocese of Lilongwe CHBC. The testing in Kamuzu central Hospital&#x2019;s short stay is a good practice in reaching the untested.

HIV testing to inmates is critical in reaching the special groups. The Lighthouse will continue with this service to link those that test HIV positive into care and support services including treatment

About 60% of chronic coughers at Martin Preaus Center test HIV positive. This knowledge of status will help in linking clients to care services and treatment. TB/HIV co infection makes them eligible for ART.

The Lighthouse would want to increase HIV ascertainment among TB suspects to 80%. Early Infant Diagnosis is a great PMTCT intervention and the programme will continue to provide HTC to the infants and link them to care services. Those that fail to return for DNA-PCR results will be followed and traced for the same.

Lighthouse commitment to HTC service quality continues with this objective. The partner observes and will continue to uphold the   counselling and testing protocols and that SOPs are being followed. This is where the partner builds its  strength to support MoH quality assurance systems.</narrative>
  </description>
